<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-AG19-102>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-AG19-102" ;
  triage:title "architecture.md still describes AckReplyDisposition::SuppressedSelfAck local-terminate behavior that hard-rejection replaced" ;
  triage:description "docs/architecture.md ~lines 1114-1136 (§6.3) still documents local self-addressed pending-ack messages terminating at (Read, Acknowledged) via AckReplyDisposition::SuppressedSelfAck. Every swept worktree instead hard-rejects local self-ack in validate_reply_target (crates/atm-core/src/ack/mod.rs), returning a validation error and leaving the source message pending. Sweep shows this hard-reject behavior is NOT introduced by AG.19: it is already present, byte-identical in wording and effect, on feature/pAG-s18-unify-envelope-handler (the earliest worktree in this ordered set) and on integrate/phase-AG (which does not yet include AG.19's own commits). git log -S on the exact error string in the s18 worktree traces its introduction to an ancestor commit outside this sprint ladder ('Unify AG15 self-host ack and smoke coverage', ce2ab044), which is already merged into every worktree in this set including s18. docs/plans/phase-AG/sprint-AG19.md does not authorize a doc-only reconciliation: it lists removing AckReplyDisposition/SuppressedSelfAck machinery as an AG.19-scope deletion target ('any split ack outcome family that forces caller/test code to reason about SuppressedSelfAck vs Sent as distinct transport behaviors' under 'Logic / Branches / State That Do Not Belong'), consistent with the code already matching that direction since AG15, but neither sprint-AG15.md nor sprint-AG19.md lists docs/architecture.md as a target file or deliverable. This is pre-existing, uniform doc/code drift dating to AG15, silently carried forward unchanged through every subsequent sprint branch swept here -- not a new or varying state-machine change specific to AG.19." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AG" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-vs-code" ;
  triage:severity "Blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;

  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-AG19-102/s18/doc> ,
                       <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-AG19-102/s18/code> ,
